# Boss (Cog_Dancers) savestate must stay intact. Loads a checked-in fixture captured from the DebugMod "Boss -
# Cogwork Dancers" reference with the two dancers damaged to non-default hp (150/120) via a direct hp set, so the hp
# assert proves the value was *restored from the snapshot* (not just the prefab default, 190). Then two independent
# loads of the same fixture, each advancing the same frames, must produce byte-identical savestates — the full boss
# capture (HealthManagers, FSMs, tk2d animators, activeSelf toggles, RNG, hazard-respawn) restores deterministically.
# A command round-trip in one frame can't work (LoadSavestate's async scene load doesn't complete before the next
# command), so both saves come from a full load + equal settle; see CLAUDE.md "Savestate load".
LoadSavestate, {tests}/savestates/cog_dancers_entry.json
   3
Assert, Equal, "{ 150, 120 }", "{HealthManager.hp}"
SaveSavestate, {scratch}.a.json
LoadSavestate, {tests}/savestates/cog_dancers_entry.json
   3
SaveSavestate, {scratch}.b.json
AssertEqualSavestates, {scratch}.a.json, {scratch}.b.json
   1
***
